From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomas Mihalicka <tomas@mihalicka.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:22:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] Persist payments in an append-only file store

Keep payments in a log file so they survive a restart. Each save
appends the payment's latest state as one JSON line and syncs it to
disk before returning. An index of byte offsets, rebuilt when the log
is opened, lets a read seek straight to a payment's newest line, and a
second index finds a payment by its tenant and idempotency key.

A crash in the middle of a save can leave a final line without its
newline. Opening the log truncates that torn line instead of refusing
to start.

Areas: infrastructure
